From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps follow ChromeOS's dark/light mode and
 accent color

NickelAppearanceReporter, owned by the host apps publisher (0012), tells
nickel-appd (org.nickelos.Apps.SetAppearance) whether the system is in
dark or light mode and which accent color it uses: at start, on every
change of Ash's color palette, and again whenever nickel-appd (re)starts.
NickelOS's xdg-desktop-portal backend passes both on to Linux apps
(Settings portal, org.freedesktop.appearance color-scheme and
accent-color), so GTK 4/libadwaita, Qt and GTK 3 apps switch with
ChromeOS.

The accent color is Ash's own primary color: tone 40 (light) or 80 (dark)
of the primary tonal palette generated from the palette seed, with Ash's
scheme-to-variant mapping.

